  "exec_summary": "The European Banking Authority has issued an email alert on August 6, 2026, which is a significant development for EU financial institutions. Additionally, the Anti-Money Laundering Authority has published draft guidelines on ongoing monitoring under Article 26(5) of the Anti-Money Laundering Regulation, providing clarity for firms on their AML obligations. In Belgium, the financial regulator has awarded a payment license to FinTech innovators, demonstrating the country's efforts to foster innovation in the financial sector. The AMLA's draft guidelines are particularly noteworthy as they aim to strengthen the EU's anti-money laundering framework.",
